🦠 The economic consequences of COVID-era policies are still being felt today. Expanding welfare programs and reducing incentives to work made it easier for millions of Americans to leave the workforce.

While the Trump administration has reversed some of those policies, there is still more work to be done to restore a culture of work and economic opportunity.

@RealEJAntoni is the Chief Economist at The Heritage Foundation.

Election integrity isn't optional. Thousands of non-citizens ended up on New Jersey's voter rolls, and hundreds reportedly cast ballots.

Americans deserve confidence that every vote cast is legal and every election is secure. Proof of citizenship to register. Voter ID to vote. It's common sense.

@lora_ries is Director of the Border Security and Immigration Center at The Heritage Foundation.

